    "## Worked example — the |+⟩ state\n",
    "\n",
    "The Hadamard gate creates a superposition from |0⟩. Before measurement, the ideal probability of 0 and 1 is 50% each. Here we use an exact statevector simulation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "954dd408",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "   ┌───┐\n",
      "q: ┤ H ├\n",
      "   └───┘\n",
      "{np.str_('0'): np.float64(0.4999999999999999), np.str_('1'): np.float64(0.4999999999999999)}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "demo = QuantumCircuit(1)\n",
    "demo.h(0)\n",
    "print(demo.draw(output=\"text\"))\n",
    "print(Statevector.from_instruction(demo).probabilities_dict())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a84f5b0a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Task 0A — Basis states (20 min)\n",
    "\n",
    "Make a one- or two-qubit basis state. **Expected:** preparing `10` produces probability 1 for `10` and zero elsewhere."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "83588a9a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def prepare_basis_state(bits: str) -> QuantumCircuit:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Create |bits⟩ using X gates. Input: '0','1','00','01','10','11'. Use Qiskit bit order; raise ValueError for any other input.\"\"\"\n",
    "    basis = QuantumCircuit(len(bits))\n",
    "    for i, bit in enumerate(bits):\n",
    "        if bit == '1':\n",
    "            basis.x(len(bits) - i - 1)\n",
    "    return basis"
   ]
  },
